  "variables": {},
  "clock": "2026-11-02T10:30:00Z",
  "touch": false
 },
 "check": {
  "describe": "10:30 UTC on 2 November: the day side is centred on Africa and Europe with the sun just south of the equator over 22.5 E; London 10:30 and Dubai 14:30 are lit (blue skies, a high sun, warm dots with a halo on the map); San Francisco 02:30, New York 05:30, Tokyo 19:30 and Sydney 21:30 are night cards with stars and a crescent. dawn (07:15 UTC): London's card is in dusk colours with the sun on its horizon, the terminator just past it. evening (19:45 UTC): the day is over the Americas, San Francisco and New York lit, Tokyo 04:45 and Sydney 06:45 read Tomorrow (Sydney's sun rising). june and december tilt the terminator opposite ways (the sun north or south of the equator). tablet (1024x640): the map wide on top, one row of six cards; tablet-portrait (800x1280) and phone: two columns, the cards taller to use the height. mono-dark and mono-light: no hue: grey land, the night side faded with its edge drawn as a line, the sun a disc in a ring, day cities filled dots with a halo and night cities hollow rings; each card an outlined rounded box with a rayed sun (day) or a crescent (night) and the time in white on black (or black on white).",
